  "problem": "What is the minor of ${a}_{12}$ in the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3d & 5b \\\\ b & {c}^{2} & b-d \\\\ b & -10c & b+d\\end{aligned}]?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we remove the first row and second column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\u2217 & -3d & \u2217 \\\\ b & \u2217 & b-d \\\\ b & \u2217 & b+d\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}b & b-d \\\\ b & b+d\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}b & b-d \\\\ b & b+d\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =b\\cdot (b+d)-(b-d)\\cdot b \\\\  & ={b}^{2}+bd-{b}^{2}+db \\\\  & =2bd\\end{aligned}\n$$",
